The ﬁgures F^{1}, F^{2}, F^{3}, and F^{4} shown are the ﬁrst in a sequence of ﬁgures. For n ≥3, F^{n} is
constructed from F^{n−1} by surrounding it with a square and placing one more diamond on each
side of the new square than F^{n−1} had on each side of its outside square. For example, ﬁgure F^{3}
has 13 diamonds. How many diamonds are there in ﬁgure F^{20}?
F^{1}
F^{2}
F^{3}
F^{4}
